1
00:00:00,975 --> 00:00:04,895
Last time, bread mould grew in our bag: a harmful fungus.

2
00:00:05,175 --> 00:00:08,045
Yeast made dough rise: a useful fungus.

3
00:00:08,315 --> 00:00:09,775
Then we washed our hands.

4
00:00:10,055 --> 00:00:10,775
Why?

5
00:00:10,956 --> 00:00:12,323
They look clean.

6
00:00:12,144 --> 00:00:13,994
I see nothing on them!

7
00:00:14,157 --> 00:00:15,517
Look closer, Pip.

8
00:00:15,847 --> 00:00:17,277
We need a microscope!

9
00:00:17,706 --> 00:00:18,946
Today you'll learn...

10
00:00:19,096 --> 00:00:20,526
How we see bacteria.

11
00:00:20,672 --> 00:00:22,582
Harmful or useful bacteria.

12
00:00:22,729 --> 00:00:24,498
The whole chapter on one map.

13
00:00:25,003 --> 00:00:26,223
Lock in first.

14
00:00:26,503 --> 00:00:28,823
A little ant is hiding in this video.

15
00:00:29,113 --> 00:00:30,312
Can you spot it?

16
00:00:30,817 --> 00:00:34,276
A microscope allows us to see very small things.

17
00:00:37,142 --> 00:00:42,562
As scientists developed more powerful microscopes, they were able to discover living

18
00:00:42,312 --> 00:00:45,122
things that are even smaller than fungi.

19
00:00:45,544 --> 00:00:46,484
Bacteria!

20
00:00:46,794 --> 00:00:47,984
Rod-shaped.

21
00:00:48,454 --> 00:00:49,544
Sphere-shaped.

22
00:00:50,014 --> 00:00:51,244
Spiral-shaped.

23
00:00:51,446 --> 00:00:52,776
One bacterium.

24
00:00:53,226 --> 00:00:54,576
Many bacteria.

25
00:00:55,230 --> 00:00:59,200
Bacteria are tiny living things and they come in different shapes and

26
00:00:58,950 --> 00:00:59,860
sizes.

27
00:00:59,998 --> 00:01:01,148
Be a bacterium!

28
00:01:01,448 --> 00:01:02,428
Shrink down.

29
00:01:02,708 --> 00:01:03,638
Quietly.

30
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:07,478
You are one bacterium.

31
00:01:07,918 --> 00:01:09,058
Rod-shaped.

32
00:01:09,478 --> 00:01:11,158
Far too small to see.

33
00:01:11,683 --> 00:01:13,323
You sit on a fingertip.

34
00:01:13,733 --> 00:01:15,423
Its lines are like hills.

35
00:01:15,947 --> 00:01:17,237
It is recess.

36
00:01:17,667 --> 00:01:19,757
The hand reaches for a sandwich.

37
00:01:20,281 --> 00:01:21,851
But first: water!

38
00:01:22,421 --> 00:01:23,171
Soap!

39
00:01:23,601 --> 00:01:25,181
The bubbles lift you off.

40
00:01:25,696 --> 00:01:26,526
Whoosh!

41
00:01:26,956 --> 00:01:28,446
Down the drain you go.

42
00:01:29,028 --> 00:01:31,138
Now the hand is ready for food.

43
00:01:32,559 --> 00:01:33,799
Bye-bye, bacteria!

44
00:01:33,989 --> 00:01:35,049
Soap wins!

45
00:01:35,476 --> 00:01:39,066
Bacteria can be harmful when they cause you to fall sick.

46
00:01:41,801 --> 00:01:44,241
So wash your hands with soap before you eat.

47
00:01:45,716 --> 00:01:46,606
Round one.

48
00:01:46,916 --> 00:01:48,626
Are all bacteria harmful?

49
00:01:48,916 --> 00:01:49,996
One, yes.

50
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:51,126
Two, no.

51
00:01:51,416 --> 00:01:52,896
Show me with your fingers.

52
00:01:58,367 --> 00:01:59,347
Locked in!

53
00:01:59,475 --> 00:02:00,095
One!

54
00:02:00,235 --> 00:02:01,645
Bacteria make us sick.

55
00:02:01,785 --> 00:02:03,105
Wash them all away!

56
00:02:03,153 --> 00:02:03,953
Two!

57
00:02:04,023 --> 00:02:05,633
Some fungi are useful.

58
00:02:05,793 --> 00:02:07,783
Maybe some bacteria are too.

59
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:08,720
Two.

60
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:10,770
I think my yoghurt has some.

61
00:02:11,983 --> 00:02:13,313
The answer is two.

62
00:02:13,739 --> 00:02:14,899
Say it with me!

63
00:02:15,608 --> 00:02:19,048
Some bacteria are harmful, while others are useful to us.

64
00:02:24,122 --> 00:02:27,852
Useful bacteria in our body help us to break down food.

65
00:02:28,072 --> 00:02:31,932
Yoghurt and yoghurt drinks have useful bacteria like these.

66
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:33,170
Two fingers?

67
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,660
One finger up!

68
00:02:36,008 --> 00:02:37,088
Pip's homework!

69
00:02:37,398 --> 00:02:38,508
Read the table.

70
00:02:38,778 --> 00:02:41,048
A has spores, and makes its own food.

71
00:02:41,338 --> 00:02:44,088
B has spores, and cannot make its own food.

72
00:02:44,358 --> 00:02:47,178
C has feathers, and cannot make its own food.

73
00:02:47,318 --> 00:02:48,478
My answers.

74
00:02:48,658 --> 00:02:50,328
One: A is a fungus.

75
00:02:50,468 --> 00:02:52,188
Two: B is a fungus.

76
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:54,028
Three: C is a bird.

77
00:02:54,305 --> 00:02:55,205
Showdown!

78
00:02:55,515 --> 00:02:56,645
Double points.

79
00:02:56,915 --> 00:02:58,535
One line has a mistake.

80
00:02:58,825 --> 00:03:00,585
Line one, two, or three?

81
00:03:00,885 --> 00:03:02,355
Show me with your fingers.

82
00:03:08,830 --> 00:03:09,810
Locked in!

83
00:03:09,938 --> 00:03:10,568
One!

84
00:03:10,708 --> 00:03:11,978
A makes its own food.

85
00:03:12,148 --> 00:03:13,888
So A is a plant, like a fern!

86
00:03:13,942 --> 00:03:14,672
One!

87
00:03:14,812 --> 00:03:16,822
Spores alone do not decide.

88
00:03:16,873 --> 00:03:17,553
Oops!

89
00:03:18,387 --> 00:03:19,777
Read every column.

90
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:23,367
Spores, and cannot make its own food: a fungus.

91
00:03:23,575 --> 00:03:24,565
One finger?

92
00:03:24,865 --> 00:03:26,765
Put up two more on your score hand!

93
00:03:27,191 --> 00:03:29,381
Now, the whole chapter on one map!

94
00:03:29,661 --> 00:03:30,771
Living things.

95
00:03:30,986 --> 00:03:33,276
Plants: flowering, and non-flowering.

96
00:03:33,476 --> 00:03:38,006
Animals: amphibians, birds, fish, insects, reptiles, mammals.

97
00:03:38,221 --> 00:03:39,041
Fungi.

98
00:03:39,321 --> 00:03:40,451
And bacteria.

99
00:03:40,728 --> 00:03:43,578
Fungi and bacteria are also living things.

100
00:03:44,738 --> 00:03:45,839
Say it with us!

101
00:03:46,499 --> 00:03:47,367
Fungi!

102
00:03:47,179 --> 00:03:48,804
Cannot make their own food!

103
00:03:52,099 --> 00:03:53,009
Bacteria!

104
00:03:52,779 --> 00:03:54,213
Tiny living things!

105
00:03:57,699 --> 00:03:59,149
Useful or harmful?

106
00:03:59,079 --> 00:04:00,275
Both can be!

107
00:04:03,904 --> 00:04:05,054
Exam corner!

108
00:04:05,327 --> 00:04:06,547
Say it with me!

109
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:11,900
Living things can be classified based on common observable characteristics.

110
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:17,180
Scientists have classified different living things into groups such as plants, animals,

111
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:18,550
fungi and bacteria.

112
00:04:21,179 --> 00:04:22,649
Show me your score hand!

113
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:23,979
More than one?

114
00:04:24,279 --> 00:04:25,639
You beat the Buddies.

115
00:04:25,939 --> 00:04:26,999
Three fingers?

116
00:04:27,269 --> 00:04:28,279
High five!

117
00:04:28,784 --> 00:04:30,184
Did you spot the ant?

118
00:04:30,434 --> 00:04:31,704
It was by the soap!

119
00:04:32,014 --> 00:04:34,424
Can you see an ant without a microscope?

120
00:04:34,684 --> 00:04:35,984
Tell someone at home.

121
00:04:36,574 --> 00:04:39,094
Next time, something new: materials!

122
00:04:39,354 --> 00:04:42,554
A plastic box, a metal box and a glass jar.

123
00:04:42,854 --> 00:04:44,904
One of them was made from sand.

124
00:04:45,174 --> 00:04:46,094
Which one?

125
00:04:46,364 --> 00:04:47,694
Lock in your answer!

126
00:04:47,965 --> 00:04:48,685
Sand?

127
00:04:48,795 --> 00:04:50,145
In my snack box?

128
00:04:50,205 --> 00:04:51,215
Crunchy!

129
00:04:51,865 --> 00:04:54,065
Let's read today's key words together!

130
00:04:54,355 --> 00:04:55,115
Ready?

131
00:04:55,402 --> 00:04:56,502
Microscope.

132
00:04:58,068 --> 00:04:58,948
Harmful.

133
00:05:00,338 --> 00:05:01,188
Useful.

134
00:05:02,558 --> 00:05:03,498
Well done!

135
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,584
Say it with us!

136
00:05:06,384 --> 00:05:07,134
Ready?

137
00:05:07,257 --> 00:05:07,917
One!

138
00:05:08,257 --> 00:05:08,957
two!

139
00:05:09,262 --> 00:05:10,437
Now you know!
